Krita Nova 15 - floating vertical Brush Panel (Android)

On Android the top bar holds New / Open / Save plus mirror/wrap, layouts and
workspaces. Undo/Redo and the rest of the "Brushes and Stuff" toolbar
(gradient, pattern, colors, brush editor, presets, blending mode, alpha
lock/reload, size, opacity) move into a floating narrow "Brush Panel".

1. KisMainWindow: createAndroidBrushPanel() adds a QDockWidget
   (objectName KritaNovaBrushPanel, Krita's dock title bar) and reparents the
   XMLGUI toolbars "editToolBar" and "BrushesAndStuff" into it, vertical and
   not movable. They stay the same XMLGUI-managed KisToolBar objects, so
   Configure Toolbars keeps working. QMainWindow::restoreState() (window
   settings, workspaces) puts known toolbars back into its toolbar layout
   without reparenting them, which left them invisible in the panel and kept
   the top bar from stretching; an event filter (ParentChange, Move, explicit
   Hide) and the panel's start-up checks take them out of the main window's
   layout again. The dock has no allowed dock areas, is re-floated when
   something docks it, and has no keyboard accelerator in its title.
2. BrushPanelShower shows the panel 400 ms after the main window is first
   shown (a floating dock is a window of its own and is not shown along with
   the main window; startup's window state / workspace restore may also hide
   or re-dock it). The first time, or whenever it is off screen, it floats at
   the left edge, tall (kritarc: androidBrushPanelPlaced2); otherwise it is
   shown where it was. Closing it hides it for the session; Settings >
   Toolbars Shown has an entry to bring it back.
3. KisToolBar::mainWindow() searches all ancestors for the main window, not
   just the direct parent; several code paths dereference it unchecked
   (context menu, saveState) and would crash for a toolbar in the panel.

4. The panel is a narrow column: the toolbar's horizontal button groups
   (brush editor/presets, blending mode/alpha lock/reload, mirror/wrap) are
   turned vertical, and the blending mode box is as wide as the column (its
   list keeps a readable width). The Opacity/Size sliders (brushslider1/2)
   are hidden and replaced by two tall vertical sliders, Size above Opacity,
   bound to the same KisDoubleSliderSpinBox objects: drag up/down to change
   the value relative to where the drag started (Size uses the same cubic
   curve as the horizontal slider); the value shows while dragging.

5. mirror_actions, select_layout and workspaces are moved from the brush
   toolbar to the top bar (mainToolBar); the expanding spacer is hidden, so
   the vertical sliders get the panel's spare height (the panel starts tall).
6. A round button at the bottom of the panel shows the foreground color.
   Tapping it switches to the Color Sampler tool; after one sample on the
   canvas (release of pen/mouse/touch on the canvas widget) it switches back
   to the previously active tool. Tapping it again cancels; choosing another
   tool by hand also cancels.

Desktop builds are unchanged.

